/**
 * @defgroup EiddGeo EiddGeo — Endcap Inner Detector (ETTIE) Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR ETTIE combined endcap detector,
 *        detector tag EIDD.
 *
 * @details
 * The ETTIE (Endcap TRD-TOF for Identifying Electrons) detector is a proposed multi-subsystem
 * endcap instrument for electron identification at the STAR west endcap, placed at z = −286 cm.
 * It covers the full TPC radial aperture (r = 46.1–206.75 cm) in twelve 28°-wide azimuthal
 * sectors.  Three sub-detectors are stacked along z within the single ETTV mother volume:
 *
 * **eTRD (Transition Radiation Detector)** — ETRV at z = 280 cm.
 * Three TRD layers, each composed of a foam TR radiator (5.92 cm), a Xe+15% CO2
 * absorber (TABS, 3.83 cm, sensitive), and a G10 readout motherboard (TBOD, 2.00 cm).
 * Transition radiation from charged particles above threshold is detected in the xenon gas.
 *
 * **eMRPC TOF** — ETFV at z = 299 cm.
 * One layer of Multi-gap Resistive Plate Chambers: aluminium gas box (TBOX) → Freon gas
 * volume (TGAS) with two G10 PCB readout boards, seven glass plates, and six Freon-filled
 * gas gaps (TGAP, 220 µm each, sensitive).  Provides time-of-flight measurement for
 * particle identification.
 *
 * **Lead-Scintillator Preshower** — ECLV at z = 305 cm.
 * Converter–scintillator sandwich per sector: 1st lead absorber (TEAA, 1.68 cm) →
 * scintillator (SCIN, 3.00 cm, sensitive) → 2nd lead absorber (TEAB, 0.84 cm) →
 * scintillator (SCIN, 3.00 cm, sensitive).  Designed to pre-shower electromagnetic
 * particles before possible further measurement.
 *
 * There is no separate Config XML for this detector; the module @c EIDDGEO is loaded
 * directly.  A single geometry version (eidConfig = 1) is implemented.
 *
 * @par Author
 * Ming Shao
 *
 * @par Created
 * 28 September 2011
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @defgroup EiddGeoETRD EIDDGEO — Endcap Transition Radiation Detector (eTRD)
 * @ingroup EiddGeo
 * @brief Three TRD layers at z = 280 cm covering r = 46.1–206.75 cm in 12 sectors.
 *
 * @details Each layer (ETRD) is a 28°-wide TUBS sector containing a foam TR radiator
 * (TRAD, Radiator mix ρ = 0.104 g/cm³), a Xe+15% CO2 absorber (TABS, sensitive), and a
 * G10 readout motherboard (TBOD).  The three layers are stacked along z at 12 cm intervals
 * within the ETRV volume.  TABS is the sensitive medium; hits record position, direction
 * cosines, momentum, path length, TOF, log(γ), step size, and energy loss.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup EiddGeoTOF EIDDGEO — Endcap MRPC Time-of-Flight (eMRPC)
 * @ingroup EiddGeo
 * @brief Single MRPC TOF layer at z = 299 cm with 7 glass plates and 6 gas gaps per sector.
 *
 * @details Each of the twelve ETOF sectors is a 28°-wide TUBS containing an aluminium gas
 * box (TBOX) and a Freon gas volume (TGAS).  Within TGAS: two G10 PCB readout boards (TPCB)
 * flank a stack of 7 glass plates (TGLA, 0.5 mm each) and 6 Freon gas gaps (TGAP, 220 µm
 * each, sensitive).  The multi-gap design provides improved time resolution.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup EiddGeoPreShower EIDDGEO — Endcap Lead-Scintillator Preshower
 * @ingroup EiddGeo
 * @brief Pb+scintillator preshower at z = 305 cm for electromagnetic particle identification.
 *
 * @details Each of the twelve TECL sectors is a 28°-wide TUBS containing a sandwich of:
 * TEAA (1.68 cm Pb), SCIN (3.00 cm polystyrene, sensitive), TEAB (0.84 cm Pb), and a
 * second SCIN (3.00 cm, sensitive).  The two scintillator layers allow shower-depth
 * estimation for electron/pion separation.
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
